From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Jonathan Goyvaerts <jonathan.goyvaerts@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 18 Oct 2026 00:42:10 -0300
Subject: [PATCH] ASoC: tas2764: do not report an unreadable interrupt latch as
 faults

The IRQ handler reads the six interrupt latch registers with
snd_soc_component_read() into a u8 array. On a failed read that
function returns the negative errno, which truncates to a byte with
most bits set: the handler then logs over-temperature, over-current and
most other faults that never happened, and the context bytes are
garbage.

Read the latches with regmap_read() and return IRQ_NONE, with a
rate-limited error, when one of them cannot be read.

Fixes: dae191fb957f ("ASoC: tas2764: Add IRQ handling")
Signed-off-by: Jonathan Goyvaerts <jonathan.goyvaerts@gmail.com>
Assisted-by: LLM
(cherry picked from commit f0e5882d6837a019b263d7a47d4a4ab48533b0f6)
Signed-off-by: Dylan Ironside <dylan@dylanironside.io>
---
 sound/soc/codecs/tas2764.c | 12 +++++++++---
 1 file changed, 9 insertions(+), 3 deletions(-)

diff --git a/sound/soc/codecs/tas2764.c b/sound/soc/codecs/tas2764.c
index 4f847e8935..080c4f4caf 100644
--- a/sound/soc/codecs/tas2764.c
+++ b/sound/soc/codecs/tas2764.c
@@ -78,12 +78,18 @@ static irqreturn_t tas2764_irq(int irq, void *data)
 {
 	struct tas2764_priv *tas2764 = data;
 	u8 latched[6] = {0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0};
+	unsigned int val;
 	int ret = IRQ_NONE;
 	int i;
 
-	for (i = 0; i < ARRAY_SIZE(latched); i++)
-		latched[i] = snd_soc_component_read(tas2764->component,
-						    tas2764_int_readout_regs[i]);
+	/* A failed read is no fault report: an errno would read as every fault bit. */
+	for (i = 0; i < ARRAY_SIZE(latched); i++) {
+		if (regmap_read(tas2764->regmap, tas2764_int_readout_regs[i], &val)) {
+			dev_err_ratelimited(tas2764->dev, "interrupt latch %d unreadable\n", i);
+			return IRQ_NONE;
+		}
+		latched[i] = val;
+	}
 
 	for (i = 0; i < 8; i++) {
 		if (latched[0] & BIT(i)) {
